WEBVTT

00:01.770 --> 00:03.730
<b>Katagiri High School</b>

00:04.050 --> 00:05.950
How'd you do on the mock exam?

00:05.950 --> 00:07.730
Not too bad.

00:08.400 --> 00:13.740
<i>Third-year high schoolers have fun, 
but we spend a lot of time studying.</i>

00:14.440 --> 00:18.990
<i>When we get home, we fight through 
reviewing our lessons and old exam problems.</i>

00:19.470 --> 00:23.000
<i>In our spare time, we study vocabulary.</i>

00:23.810 --> 00:27.370
<i>My singular reprieve
from the daily grind is...</i>

00:28.420 --> 00:30.760
<b>The super popular {red}KONOHA
{blue}will be adapted into an anime!</b>

00:30.160 --> 00:32.180
<i>reading manga!</i>

00:32.180 --> 00:34.130
<i>It's the highlight of my week.</i>

00:36.760 --> 00:38.250
<i>He's a double agent?!</i>

00:38.250 --> 00:41.190
<i>Wait, how?! I never saw that coming!</i>

00:41.190 --> 00:43.770
<i>I thought he was just going 
through his daily routine!</i>

00:43.770 --> 00:46.270
<b>A friendship betrayed...
What will happen to Konoha?!</b>

00:43.770 --> 00:46.270
<b>To be continued next week</b>

00:44.810 --> 00:46.260
<i>No kidding!</i>

00:48.840 --> 00:51.610
<i>Next week can't come soon enough!</i>

02:29.450 --> 02:31.630
You're sure in high spirits, Sakura.

02:32.280 --> 02:34.040
I'm heading home!

02:35.850 --> 02:39.660
<i>The next </i>Konoha<i>! The next </i>Konoha<i>!</i>

02:39.660 --> 02:43.580
<i>The next </i>Konoha<i>! The next </i>Konoha<i>!</i>

02:43.580 --> 02:47.770
<i>The next </i>Konoha<i>! The next </i>Konoha<i>!</i>

02:47.770 --> 02:48.770
<b>Empty</b>

02:52.450 --> 02:53.950
E-Excuse me...

02:53.950 --> 02:56.260
Did you get the new <i><i>Weekly Shinobi</i></i> today?

02:56.260 --> 02:57.780
Huh? Oh.

02:57.780 --> 03:00.490
We just sold out of it.

03:03.920 --> 03:05.560
Should we put one on backorder?

03:05.560 --> 03:07.540
No, thank you.

03:08.390 --> 03:11.720
<i>The convenience stores always 
sell out on release day,</i>

03:11.720 --> 03:13.570
<i>so I came straight to the book store.</i>

03:14.130 --> 03:16.050
The next <i>Konoha</i>...

03:19.600 --> 03:20.530
<i>I can't take it!</i>

03:19.880 --> 03:25.300
AAAAAGH

03:20.530 --> 03:24.770
<i>After thinking about </i>Konoha<i> all day, 
the shock might just kill me!</i>

03:24.770 --> 03:25.300
Huh?

03:26.080 --> 03:27.140
Kono-san?

03:29.120 --> 03:30.700
Y-Yanagi-kun!

03:30.700 --> 03:31.810
What is it?

03:31.810 --> 03:33.640
<i>He saw me being weird.</i>

03:34.060 --> 03:36.470
Are you looking for the new <i>Weekly Shinobi</i>?

03:36.470 --> 03:38.750
H-How did you know?

03:39.070 --> 03:43.490
You were talking about "the next <i>Konoha</i>."

03:45.810 --> 03:47.280
<i>How embarrassing...</i>

03:47.280 --> 03:50.400
Um, you can have this if you'd like.

03:52.570 --> 03:54.640
I haven't opened it yet.

03:56.160 --> 03:57.080
But...

03:57.080 --> 04:00.710
Oh, don't worry about me.

04:01.220 --> 04:05.010
I just came in to kill time 
until my bus comes.

04:05.010 --> 04:08.430
It was the last copy,
so I felt compelled to buy it.

04:08.970 --> 04:13.260
The station I'm going to has 
lots of books, so I'll be fine.

04:14.510 --> 04:17.150
My bus will be here soon, so I've gotta go.

04:17.150 --> 04:18.920
Th-Thank you!

04:19.360 --> 04:22.040
I'll pay you back tomorrow.

04:22.040 --> 04:24.290
Yanagi-kun, um...

04:24.290 --> 04:25.940
You're...

04:26.800 --> 04:28.120
just like Kaoru-san!

04:28.780 --> 04:32.620
<b>SPARKLE</b>

04:28.780 --> 04:32.620
<b>Mysterious 
but helpful</b>

04:28.780 --> 04:32.620
<b>Kind to friends
and foes alike</b>

04:28.780 --> 04:32.620
<b>{bottom}Kaoru-san</b>

04:28.780 --> 04:32.620
A character from <b><i>Skull Ninja Konoha</i></b>. Nin-nin!

04:33.410 --> 04:35.880
Er, thank you...

04:35.880 --> 04:37.130
<i>He's weirded out!</i>

04:37.130 --> 04:40.670
<i>I compared him to one of 
the characters and he froze!</i>

04:40.670 --> 04:42.880
<i>Why did I have to go and say that?</i>

04:47.680 --> 04:50.640
<b>A mysterious woman</b>

04:47.960 --> 04:50.640
<i>Kaoru-san's a female character!</i>

04:48.070 --> 04:50.640
<b>Ya need some help?</b>

04:51.130 --> 04:53.350
<i>Is she saying I'm effeminate?</i>

04:53.820 --> 04:55.190
<i>I'd better be careful.</i>

04:55.520 --> 04:59.770
<b>SHOCK</b>

04:55.860 --> 04:59.680
<i>I weirded him out.
He's definitely weirded out.</i>

04:59.680 --> 05:00.320
Oh.

05:07.910 --> 05:10.920
<i>I guess Yanagi-kun reads manga, too.</i>

05:15.670 --> 05:16.540
Kono-san!

05:17.540 --> 05:19.400
Oh, Yanagi-kun.

05:19.830 --> 05:21.410
Are you going to the bookstore?

05:21.410 --> 05:22.090
Yes.

05:22.440 --> 05:24.720
It's <i>Weekly Shinobi</i> release day!

05:27.770 --> 05:31.390
I just can't put down <i>Konoha</i> lately!

05:31.390 --> 05:32.620
I hear that.

05:32.980 --> 05:35.870
I usually wait for the full-book publication,

05:35.870 --> 05:39.180
but once I start reading the weekly 
magazines, I can't stop.

05:39.180 --> 05:40.450
Exactly!

05:40.450 --> 05:42.340
They sure don't look like a couple.

05:43.940 --> 05:46.010
<i>I haven't heard that in a while!</i>

05:44.070 --> 05:45.990
SNAP

05:46.010 --> 05:49.200
<i>I've been hanging around with 
Hori's group so long I forgot.</i>

05:50.130 --> 05:51.850
<i>Sh-Should I be about this far?</i>

05:52.450 --> 05:53.770
Did I upset you?

05:53.770 --> 05:55.180
No, it's not like that!

05:55.180 --> 05:56.710
It's, um...

05:56.710 --> 06:02.030
If I walk next to you, it'll, um... 
make the other girls jealous.

06:05.120 --> 06:06.240
Why?

06:06.760 --> 06:08.890
Because you're such a cool guy.

06:09.890 --> 06:11.600
<i>Cool?</i>

06:11.600 --> 06:14.780
Sakura, I got a paper cut!

06:14.780 --> 06:16.880
Think of something fun.

06:16.880 --> 06:18.690
We get to go home early today!

06:18.690 --> 06:20.510
Oh? Yay!

06:20.510 --> 06:21.750
It's gone.

06:21.750 --> 06:24.240
It was just a bug. Nothing to cry about.

06:24.240 --> 06:25.540
I'm not crying...

06:25.540 --> 06:28.170
Is it really gone? For real?

06:28.170 --> 06:29.900
You're far cooler!

06:29.900 --> 06:31.400
What? Me?

06:31.760 --> 06:33.330
Wh-What are you saying?

06:33.330 --> 06:36.060
You're obviously much cooler than me.

06:36.060 --> 06:39.260
No, I think I'd want you 
there if I got hurt.

06:39.260 --> 06:40.660
What does that mean?

06:41.760 --> 06:44.180
<i>Yanagi-kun's a good guy...</i>

06:44.180 --> 06:45.300
<i>but he can be a bit odd.</i>

06:45.640 --> 06:47.130
<i>Paper cut...</i>

06:47.130 --> 06:49.900
<i>Moreover, if I had to choose...</i>

06:49.900 --> 06:53.140
<i>I'd prefer being c-c-cute over cool.</i>

06:54.050 --> 06:56.690
By the way, I haven't seen you 
wear your glasses lately.

06:56.690 --> 07:00.140
Oh, they don't really look good on me.

07:00.140 --> 07:02.060
Besides, I have contacts.

07:03.020 --> 07:06.110
<i>There's no way anything 
doesn't look good on you.</i>

07:06.110 --> 07:08.650
Really, I just want a new design.

07:08.990 --> 07:10.960
Maybe I'll go check out frames later.

07:10.960 --> 07:14.910
<i>Yanagi-kun's face is so delicate that
it makes mine stand out even more!</i>

07:15.430 --> 07:17.090
Want to come with, Kono-san?

07:17.090 --> 07:18.710
Huh? Where?

07:18.710 --> 07:19.740
To check out frames.

07:19.740 --> 07:20.760
Frames?

07:20.760 --> 07:22.910
C-Can I really tag along?

07:22.910 --> 07:24.680
If you're busy, don't sweat it.

07:24.680 --> 07:25.990
I-I'm coming!

07:26.670 --> 07:28.470
<i>What a casual invitation.</i>

07:28.470 --> 07:31.680
<i>Who could turn Yanagi-kun down?</i>

07:34.740 --> 07:37.070
I just thought of something.

07:38.760 --> 07:41.740
"Yanagi" and "Sakura" are both kinds of trees.

07:41.740 --> 07:44.190
Er, not that it means anything.

07:50.940 --> 07:52.970
No more!

07:51.110 --> 07:57.870
<b>RUUUUUUUUUUN</b>

07:52.970 --> 07:55.340
Huh? Kono-san, why are you running?

07:55.340 --> 07:56.950
Are you worried they'll be sold out?

07:56.950 --> 07:57.870
<b>Running seemed
the best option</b>

07:58.700 --> 08:00.080
<b>That's a good color.</b>

07:59.560 --> 08:01.380
<i>Everything looks good on him.</i>

08:00.120 --> 08:01.330
<b>You mean it?</b>

08:00.950 --> 08:02.660
<b>Maybe I'll 
buy these.</b>

08:02.710 --> 08:03.710
<b>I'm Her</b>

08:02.710 --> 08:06.710
A guy and a girl swap bodies!

08:03.710 --> 08:04.710
<b>She's Me</b>

08:07.170 --> 08:08.820
What book is that?

08:08.820 --> 08:11.170
Oh, I remember this one!

08:11.170 --> 08:12.290
It's really good.

08:12.290 --> 08:13.500
What is it?

08:12.290 --> 08:15.090
Posture, Yoshikawa!

08:13.500 --> 08:15.090
That <i>I'm Her</i> thing.

08:15.090 --> 08:17.040
They made a TV drama out of it.

08:17.040 --> 08:19.130
Really? I didn't see it.

08:19.130 --> 08:22.280
<i>If Hori and Miyamura swapped bodies...</i>

08:25.280 --> 08:27.950
What's that supposed to mean, Toru?

08:27.950 --> 08:29.360
Now, now...

08:29.610 --> 08:30.440
<i>Whoa!</i>

08:30.440 --> 08:31.340
<i>Is she okay?</i>

08:31.340 --> 08:32.610
Hey!

08:32.610 --> 08:35.070
Someone left their pencil case 
in the student council room.

08:35.070 --> 08:37.130
Oh, maybe it's Shu's.

08:35.740 --> 08:36.570
<b>Shu...</b>

08:37.130 --> 08:38.610
Did anyone forget a pencil case?

08:42.260 --> 08:43.740
There you go again, Ishikawa!

08:43.740 --> 08:46.550
Man, you're noisy. Pipe down.

08:48.310 --> 08:49.000
The heck?!

08:49.000 --> 08:51.280
Oh, here you are, Sengoku-kun.

08:51.830 --> 08:55.260
That case belongs to a second-year 
on next year's student council.

08:55.260 --> 08:57.710
I'm glad we found the owner.

08:58.590 --> 09:01.160
Let's go to a cake buffet later!

09:01.160 --> 09:04.050
We've got cram school first. Jeez...

09:05.710 --> 09:07.290
What's with her?

09:07.780 --> 09:10.230
She keeps humming to herself.

09:10.230 --> 09:11.650
Let's just leave her be.

09:12.020 --> 09:16.480
It's 'cause Hori was him, 
and then Remi-chan and Kono-san...

09:15.170 --> 09:18.410
Knock it off. It's getting old.

09:20.330 --> 09:22.640
I have cooking class next!

09:22.640 --> 09:24.250
Nice. Knock 'em dead.

09:24.790 --> 09:25.890
Oh, yeah!

09:25.890 --> 09:27.090
What is this?!

09:28.770 --> 09:32.300
<i>But if </i>we<i> traded places, what would 
I do in the restroom or the bath?</i>

09:32.300 --> 09:33.650
<i>Guys and girls can't go together...</i>

09:33.650 --> 09:35.050
What's going on, Yoshikawa?

09:35.050 --> 09:36.300
You can come back now.

09:36.890 --> 09:38.500
What about the restroom?!

09:38.500 --> 09:40.430
The restroom?! What about it?!

09:40.850 --> 09:43.210
If you need to use it, just go.

09:43.210 --> 09:44.720
It's not good to hold it too long.

09:45.180 --> 09:47.950
It's way more complicated than that.

09:47.950 --> 09:49.330
Huh?

09:48.190 --> 09:50.190
<b>Confusion</b>

09:50.190 --> 09:52.190
<b>Library</b>

09:52.190 --> 09:55.190
I'm sure it would feel weird 
for you to call me by my first name.

09:57.200 --> 09:58.480
Kyoko-chan.

09:57.200 --> 10:01.950
<b>Shudder</b>

09:59.040 --> 10:00.570
Kyoko-chan!

10:01.950 --> 10:04.300
This is no time for goofing off.

10:04.300 --> 10:05.680
I'll go buy some writing paper.

10:05.680 --> 10:07.080
See ya.

10:07.540 --> 10:09.490
Hori, get some pencil lead, too!

10:09.490 --> 10:10.900
Okay!

10:10.080 --> 10:13.340
<b>Library</b>

10:25.590 --> 10:27.600
<i>I forgot to ask for more red pens!</i>

10:38.050 --> 10:40.350
I didn't think anyone else was here.

10:40.350 --> 10:42.460
Oh, I, um...

10:42.460 --> 10:43.490
Sorry.

10:43.490 --> 10:44.530
It's okay.

10:44.870 --> 10:46.620
I got here just as Hori-san was leaving.

10:48.710 --> 10:50.370
This book is cold.

10:51.160 --> 10:52.060
Huh?

10:53.090 --> 10:54.130
It's nothing.

10:59.880 --> 11:02.160
Your hand is just too warm, Yoshikawa-san.

11:06.800 --> 11:08.860
<i>The backs of our hands touched.</i>

11:09.770 --> 11:11.480
Thanks

11:09.970 --> 11:13.070
<i>Yanagi-kun's hand felt so cold...</i>

11:10.770 --> 11:12.480
No prob

11:17.780 --> 11:20.280
Hey, did you finish your report?

11:20.280 --> 11:21.650
My hand's cold.

11:21.650 --> 11:22.530
Huh?

11:22.530 --> 11:25.030
My hand's really cold.

11:25.030 --> 11:26.790
What?

11:27.290 --> 11:28.930
Feels pretty warm to me.

11:27.290 --> 11:30.540
SQUEEZE
SQUEEZE

11:28.930 --> 11:30.540
Mine's way colder.

11:30.540 --> 11:33.290
Y-You don't need to grab 
and touch it that much!

11:33.560 --> 11:35.130
What?

11:35.380 --> 11:35.920
<b>PRESS</b>

11:35.380 --> 11:38.380
You're such a pain! 
What'd you expect me to do?

11:38.380 --> 11:42.130
Y-Y-Yanagi-kun doesn't touch me like this!

11:42.840 --> 11:44.930
So you don't want me doing it?

11:44.930 --> 11:46.760
That's not what I said.

11:47.010 --> 11:48.240
What a pain in the neck!

11:48.240 --> 11:50.770
I don't get you, Yoshikawa. 
You're such a headache.

11:51.020 --> 11:52.230
<b><i>SNAP</i></b>

11:51.020 --> 11:53.120
Yoshikawa, you are seriously a pain!

11:52.770 --> 11:57.150
<b>More or less 
honest</b>

11:53.120 --> 11:54.280
I'm not messing around!

11:54.280 --> 11:57.160
I-I thought you <i>were</i> messing around!

11:57.770 --> 11:59.080
Have you warmed up?

11:59.080 --> 12:01.730
Yeah, but now I'm tired.

12:01.730 --> 12:03.420
It's from writing that report.

12:03.880 --> 12:05.330
Time to go home.

12:08.060 --> 12:08.920
Wanna hold hands?

12:08.920 --> 12:10.160
Not a chance.

12:10.410 --> 12:12.500
I don't get you.

12:12.980 --> 12:15.420
<i>Toru's hands are cold, too.</i>

12:16.170 --> 12:19.040
<i>But when he's with me, they warm up.</i>

12:22.250 --> 12:24.260
Miyamura, are you headed out?

12:24.260 --> 12:27.530
Yeah, I need to stop by the store.

12:28.010 --> 12:28.970
See ya.

12:28.970 --> 12:29.880
Yeah.

12:32.990 --> 12:35.020
Man, it's cold.

12:44.780 --> 12:45.930
Sawada?

12:58.790 --> 13:00.070
<i>For real?</i>

13:03.440 --> 13:04.550
Sawada.

13:05.090 --> 13:07.820
Don't you have any friends?

13:08.370 --> 13:09.550
Why?

13:10.020 --> 13:11.690
You're asking <i>me</i> why?

13:12.060 --> 13:15.050
Well, at least tell me 
if you're being bullied.

13:19.430 --> 13:21.560
Okay, you don't need to tell me,

13:21.560 --> 13:25.070
but it looks like those kids on the third 
floor threw your scarf out the window.

13:25.680 --> 13:28.540
Walk over to me if I'm right.

13:40.000 --> 13:41.090
Okay.

13:54.800 --> 13:57.220
Hey, what was that? Did you do something?

13:57.220 --> 13:58.220
Who knows?

13:59.250 --> 14:01.440
I didn't say anything.

14:01.860 --> 14:03.860
Did he just mouth "Die, uggos" at us?!

14:03.860 --> 14:06.860
Now I'm pissed! Who does he think he is?!

14:07.790 --> 14:11.870
So... you're being bullied, huh?

14:14.610 --> 14:18.100
I just had a different opinion 
than everyone else.

14:18.100 --> 14:21.630
Then they suddenly started ignoring me.

14:22.440 --> 14:24.040
That's how things are sometimes.

14:26.710 --> 14:28.630
You don't know how it feels.

14:28.950 --> 14:31.510
You've got tons of friends!

14:34.030 --> 14:39.040
It's not like I went around begging 
each of them to be my friend.

14:40.340 --> 14:43.170
Things are bound to get better for you.

14:44.150 --> 14:47.640
You can just ignore those idiots.

14:47.640 --> 14:48.590
And then...

14:48.590 --> 14:52.070
When they beg you to be friends with them,

14:52.070 --> 14:53.780
you'll have won.

14:53.780 --> 14:56.540
Wh-What does winning get me?

14:56.860 --> 14:58.510
I figured you wanted to win.

14:58.510 --> 14:59.860
I don't care!

15:03.050 --> 15:03.790
Oh...

15:04.220 --> 15:06.410
I accidentally stepped on your scarf.

15:07.880 --> 15:10.050
Hey, ow! Stop!

15:12.470 --> 15:15.310
Sawada-san sure gets along 
with the third-years.

15:15.310 --> 15:18.500
She must like talking to them 
more than her classmates.

15:18.500 --> 15:21.830
I know what you mean. Every time—

15:22.180 --> 15:23.500
She's looking at us.

15:23.500 --> 15:24.600
Yikes.

15:26.280 --> 15:27.760
<i>I don't care.</i>

15:32.120 --> 15:35.110
<i>It's not that I don't want 
to get along with them.</i>

15:35.110 --> 15:37.970
<i>I just don't know how.</i>

15:39.580 --> 15:43.450
<i>It makes being in class uncomfortable.</i>

15:44.230 --> 15:45.910
The wind's so strong!

15:45.910 --> 15:47.360
Oh, Sawada-san!

15:48.460 --> 15:49.980
It's so cold...

15:49.980 --> 15:53.720
Sawada-san, come inside. It's cold out here.

15:55.840 --> 15:57.850
What were you doing out there?

15:58.470 --> 16:00.350
Am I weird?

16:02.480 --> 16:04.140
Yeah, pretty much.

16:04.980 --> 16:07.980
But being a little weird is wonderful.

16:10.840 --> 16:12.230
Did something happen?

16:12.230 --> 16:13.870
Not exactly.

16:13.870 --> 16:15.990
And if <i>you're</i> weird, then...

16:15.990 --> 16:18.240
What about Remi-chan?

16:15.990 --> 16:18.240
What about Yuki-chan?

16:22.970 --> 16:24.570
Sawada-san, you can have this.

16:24.570 --> 16:26.950
It's stag beetle candy.
It tastes like stag beetles!

16:26.950 --> 16:29.250
You don't have to take it, Sawada-san.

16:29.810 --> 16:31.510
I-I'll take it.

16:31.510 --> 16:33.820
See how popular stag beetles are?

16:33.820 --> 16:35.510
Is popularity really the issue?

16:35.510 --> 16:37.390
D-Do I...

16:38.290 --> 16:42.270
get along with third-years too well?

16:42.590 --> 16:45.160
Huh? What's wrong with that?

16:46.690 --> 16:50.150
I don't really have any friends 
in my own grade.

16:50.150 --> 16:51.450
So...

16:51.900 --> 16:54.050
Ah, that's rough.

16:54.050 --> 16:56.270
There's always a lot of group work.

16:56.270 --> 16:58.030
And girls pick their groups quickly.

16:58.030 --> 16:59.740
Y-Yeah!

16:59.740 --> 17:01.660
That's it. That's exactly it.

17:03.660 --> 17:06.980
Um, Sawada-san, are you 
having trouble with your class?

17:06.980 --> 17:08.040
Are you okay?

17:08.040 --> 17:10.990
Th-Things are tough, but I'm still okay!

17:10.990 --> 17:12.140
Yeah?

17:12.140 --> 17:13.170
Yeah.

17:13.650 --> 17:16.680
If you aren't enjoying yourself, 
you can come tell us about it.

17:17.170 --> 17:22.180
We're not in your class, so hearing 
you out is about all we can do.

17:22.580 --> 17:24.200
Come by anytime!

17:24.200 --> 17:25.690
Thank you!

17:26.810 --> 17:29.040
How about a drone beetle chocolate next?

17:29.040 --> 17:30.310
It tastes like drone beetles!

17:30.310 --> 17:30.790
What?

17:30.790 --> 17:33.250
You don't have to take it, Sawada-san.

17:33.890 --> 17:39.150
<i>I'm not really comfortable in my 
class, but I still like school.</i>

17:39.700 --> 17:42.450
<b>{top}ART CLUB
<u>Beginners welcome!</u>
Watercolors, oil paints, sketches...</b>

17:40.510 --> 17:42.450
Where should we put this up?

17:42.450 --> 17:45.830
If only we'd reserved some 
space on the bulletin board...

17:45.830 --> 17:46.710
Yeah.

17:47.030 --> 17:48.330
Shimoda!

17:48.330 --> 17:51.090
Do you know any bulletin 
boards that aren't full?

17:51.090 --> 17:53.520
Sure. What about the one 
at the main entrance?

17:53.520 --> 17:55.590
The third-years use that one!

17:55.590 --> 17:56.660
They'll get mad at us!

17:56.660 --> 17:57.400
Really?

17:57.400 --> 18:00.600
<i>Recruiting for clubs seems hard.</i>

18:02.600 --> 18:04.060
<b>{top}ART CLUB
<u>Beginners welcome!</u></b>

18:07.100 --> 18:08.850
I didn't know that.

18:09.190 --> 18:10.360
And afterward...

18:11.160 --> 18:12.350
Sawada-san?

18:13.700 --> 18:16.700
You were trying to fix that poster?

18:17.270 --> 18:20.170
They're supposed to be
completely within the frame.

18:20.170 --> 18:22.450
Sengoku-kun, there's a pushpin on the floor.

18:22.450 --> 18:26.010
Yeah, the frame's pretty hard,
so it wouldn't go in deep enough.

18:26.010 --> 18:27.620
A-Actually...

18:28.190 --> 18:30.740
That poster is my friends'—

18:30.740 --> 18:32.320
My classmates'—

18:32.320 --> 18:35.130
Um, I mean...

18:35.710 --> 18:38.420
It's for a club some people in my class are in.

18:38.420 --> 18:41.210
They said they're having trouble recruiting.

18:41.210 --> 18:47.020
I think they made it big so 
it would stand out, so...

18:47.580 --> 18:50.280
Maybe it could stay up?

18:52.930 --> 18:54.040
I'm taking it down.

18:55.000 --> 18:56.600
This will be hard without a chair.

18:56.600 --> 18:59.650
Should I get one from the home ec room?

19:00.280 --> 19:01.900
I wonder if it's unlocked.

19:03.530 --> 19:04.930
I'll take it down!

19:04.930 --> 19:06.050
Stand aside, Sengoku!

19:06.050 --> 19:08.410
Hey, you know you can't reach it!

19:10.590 --> 19:11.790
Huh?

19:11.790 --> 19:13.300
Stop moving! You're scaring me!

19:11.790 --> 19:14.670
<b>Passerby Y</b>

19:12.780 --> 19:15.310
<i>They look like a family on their day off.</i>

19:13.300 --> 19:15.310
I can't.

19:15.310 --> 19:17.050
<i>Stay strong, Sengoku.</i>

19:15.310 --> 19:17.050
Pass me the pushpin.

19:17.390 --> 19:18.520
I got it off.

19:18.520 --> 19:19.620
You can put me down.

19:19.620 --> 19:20.800
Okay!

19:21.540 --> 19:23.370
Next stop!

19:23.370 --> 19:25.560
What? Hey, wait. Where are we going?

19:25.560 --> 19:28.560
Put me down! I got the poster off.

19:28.960 --> 19:29.790
You're heavy.

19:29.790 --> 19:31.560
Then hurry up and put me down!

19:31.950 --> 19:33.400
Here we are!

19:39.320 --> 19:40.850
<i>The main entrance.</i>

19:40.850 --> 19:43.200
Hand me the poster. I'll put it up.

19:43.200 --> 19:44.140
Huh?

19:44.140 --> 19:48.950
No matter how big it is, no one's 
going to see it in that secluded spot.

19:48.950 --> 19:51.210
Remi, put that one over there.

19:51.210 --> 19:51.700
Right.

19:51.700 --> 19:55.060
And then, look, there's enough space here.

19:58.860 --> 20:01.970
I thought that second-years 
couldn't use this bulletin board.

20:01.970 --> 20:03.180
Why not?

20:03.180 --> 20:06.590
Huh? Because the third-years 
are always using it.

20:06.590 --> 20:08.720
This is a shared space.

20:08.720 --> 20:11.280
I thought we'd get in trouble if we used it.

20:11.280 --> 20:12.350
Really?!

20:12.350 --> 20:17.360
Then I guess we'll need a poster that says 
any grade can use this bulletin board.

20:18.840 --> 20:19.610
All done.

20:19.610 --> 20:22.110
<b>{top}ART CLUB
<u>Beginners welcome!</u>
Watercolors, oil paints, sketches. and sculpting
Come check it out anytime!
See the art room for details</b>

20:24.630 --> 20:28.120
Now every student who comes 
through the door will see it.

20:28.120 --> 20:30.870
I hope some people come check it out.

20:31.940 --> 20:34.500
Remiremi-senpai, thank you so much!

20:34.870 --> 20:36.000
Sengoku!

20:38.980 --> 20:40.260
Thanks.

20:41.550 --> 20:42.550
Don't mention it.

20:43.260 --> 20:45.210
Say, Sawada-san, would you like candy?

20:45.210 --> 20:46.510
Not right now.

20:46.510 --> 20:48.490
How about some stag beetle chocolate?

20:55.210 --> 20:56.440
Sawada-san.

20:58.520 --> 21:03.570
I heard you rehung our 
recruitment poster. Is that true?

21:03.570 --> 21:07.140
Shimoda said he saw you do it 
two days ago after school.

21:07.140 --> 21:08.410
<i>He saw me?!</i>

21:10.710 --> 21:15.060
I-It's not like that. It was put up 
where it shouldn't have been,

21:15.060 --> 21:17.820
so I moved it to a suitable place.

21:17.820 --> 21:19.540
And it wasn't really me...

21:19.990 --> 21:22.550
A first-year came by to check out the club.

21:24.910 --> 21:26.750
That was all, sure...

21:26.750 --> 21:30.200
But we've never had a first-year come before!

21:30.200 --> 21:33.640
When I heard they saw the poster,
 I was really surprised.

21:35.060 --> 21:37.560
But it made me really happy.

21:37.960 --> 21:39.930
Thank you, Sawada-san.

21:41.510 --> 21:42.320
I...

21:43.080 --> 21:46.590
I hope you get someone to sign up next time!

21:47.240 --> 21:48.180
Yeah.

21:50.220 --> 21:51.700
Oh, and I wanted to ask...

21:52.580 --> 21:57.180
Is it true you used the council 
president to get around?

21:57.900 --> 22:00.780
N-No! Well, actually, yes.

21:57.960 --> 22:10.010
<b>Friends</b>

22:00.780 --> 22:04.920
So the class president's arms 
and legs may as well be your own?

22:04.920 --> 22:07.620
And you're related to that 
third-year with piercings?

22:07.620 --> 22:10.010
No!

22:15.220 --> 22:16.770
<b>Konoha!!</b>

22:26.030 --> 22:29.030
<i>Skull Ninja
</i>Konoha

22:55.010 --> 22:55.450
Clang

22:55.240 --> 22:55.600
<b>Gyan</b>

22:55.600 --> 22:56.770
<b><i>Punished</i></b>

23:36.760 --> 23:40.020
Konoha dances
 yet again tonight

23:36.760 --> 23:40.020
<b>To be continued next week</b>

23:36.760 --> 23:40.020
Next time
page.8 Yanagi-kun
